\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0 Need has to do with overcoming a weakness\~within\~the character. A hero with a need is always paralyzed in some way at the beginning of the story by his weakness. Desire is a goal\~outside\~the character. Once the hero comes up with his desire, he is moving in a particular direction and taking actions to reach his goal.}{ }
\par\plain 
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0 Need lets the audience see how the hero must change to have a better life.}{ It is the key to the whole story, but it remains hidden, under the surface.}
\par\plain 
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {Desire gives the audience something to want along with the hero, something they can all be moving toward through the various twists and turns\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and even digressions\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 of the story. Desire is on the surface and is what the audience thinks the story is about.}}